#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0405 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "One subject, two parameters, a different ATOXDSCH per parameter -- legal, because each (USUBJID, PARAMCD) group holds one distinct value. Discriminating fixture for the PARAMCD half of the key: drop PARAMCD and the four rows become one subject group with a 2-vs-2 tie and all four would fire. Deliberate complement of PMDA-AD0403-valid_different_subjects-ADLBC.cdt, which discriminates the USUBJID half."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col PARAMCD  type=Char
col AVISITN  type=Num
col AVAL     type=Num
col ATOXDSCH type=Char
---
S1 | 001 | GLUC | 1 | 5.0 | GRADE1
S1 | 001 | GLUC | 2 | 5.1 | GRADE1
S1 | 001 | ALB  | 1 | 4.0 | GRADE3
S1 | 001 | ALB  | 2 | 4.1 | GRADE3
